# clang-tidy check set, run by `make tidy` (the commit gate) - see AGENTS.md.
# Findings are triaged one by one: fix the code, or a // NOLINT(check) at the
# site. No check-wide disables here without an attached reason.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  cert-*,
  misc-*,
  readability-function-size,
  readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name,
  readability-suspicious-call-argument
CheckOptions:
  # glibc's public headers (getopt.h, time.h, pthread.h) are thin wrappers
  # over bits/ internals, but include-cleaner can't walk up to the public
  # header and suggests the non-self-contained bits/ files directly. Never
  # suggest those; where the public header still trips the check, a
  # // NOLINT(misc-include-cleaner) sits on the include line.
  - key: misc-include-cleaner.IgnoreHeaders
    value: 'bits/.*'
# bugprone-signed-bitwise is off: the codebase bit-packs demodulated nibbles
# and CRC/Hamming words on `int` (C integer promotion makes `uint8_t << 4`
# signed regardless of the operand types). The check targets C++ signed
# shift/mask overflow; in C these operations are well-defined at the magnitudes
# used, and qualifying all 130 sites unsigned would be churn without safety.
# If a bitwise bug is ever suspected, re-enable the check and triage afresh.
